---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { listedPosts } from './_posts.js';

// jeyanandan.com -- Jason's personal site, and only that.
//
// 2026-09-21: rewritten, at Jason's request, to a very minimal page: who I am,
// what I have released, what I am working on, the writing, and one Ko-fi link.
// The copy was written and signed off before this file was touched; it is
// placed here verbatim. Do not add a tagline, a CTA or another section.
//
// THE WRITING LIST IS GENERATED. It reads listedPosts from ./_posts.js, the
// same list /blog/ and /sitemap.xml read, so an unlisted post (fuckarian,
// the-constraint) cannot appear here while it is hidden there. Each entry is
// the post's own frontmatter: title and subtitle joined with a colon, the form
// the post pages use in their <title>, then its description.
//
// MADDIE. The only Maddie content on this page is the one For Maddie line, the
// bristlecone mark and the outbound link to formaddie.com. The demonstration,
// the recorder, the privacy policy, sign-in and the auth callbacks stay off the
// site; they are kept, unbuilt, in src/_suppressed/ and the recorder component,
// unimported, at src/components/Talk.astro. Read src/_suppressed/README.md
// before restoring any of it. The mark is self-hosted under /assets/ because
// the CSP is img-src 'self' data:. Do not swap in formaddie-rabbit.svg: its
// fill is near-white and it disappears on this paper background.
//
// TWO DEPLOY GATES. deploy-jeyanandan.yml greps the BUILT page for:
//
//     not the Foundation and not the company.
//     ko-fi.com/jeyanandan
//
// The first is the end of the opening paragraph, the second is the closing
// link. Both must stay real body text on one source line each. Reword either
// and the workflow has to change in the same change-set, workflow first.
//
// Comments in the markup below are {/* ... */}, never <!-- ... -->. Astro
// emits an HTML comment nested inside an element straight into the built page,
// and a gate sentence living in a shipped comment would pass the grep happily
// while the paragraph it was meant to guard was gone.

const postTitle = (p) => (p.subtitle ? `${p.title}: ${p.subtitle}` : p.title);
---
<Base
  title="Jason Jeyanandan"
  description="I build things, mostly for myself first, and publish the ones that hold up."
>
  <section class="hero"><div class="shell narrow">
    <h1>Jason Jeyanandan</h1>
    <div class="rule"></div>
    <p class="lede">I build things, mostly for myself first, and publish the ones that hold up. This is my personal site — not the Foundation and not the company.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section><div class="shell narrow">
    <h2 class="eyebrow">Released</h2>
    <p><strong><a href="https://github.com/ObsidianDelta/Fuckery">Fuckery</a></strong> — a framework about constraint and emergence. Structure forms under constraint, then becomes the constraint on whatever forms next. Named so that nobody genuflects at it. v0.51, CC BY 4.0.</p>
    <p><strong><a href="https://github.com/daxfoundation/constraint-protocol">The Constraint Protocol</a></strong> — people call it a ledger, which is accurate and leaves out most of it. Yes, it keeps a signed record nobody can quietly edit. It also makes each party say in advance what it will not do, keeps the witness separate from the participants and the judging separate from the witnessing, lets a declared constraint hold back certain work and note anyone who tries to skip it, lets anyone dispute anything, and lets the past be judged again without being rewritten. People, companies and software get treated the same. v0.5, a public working draft, run once so far.</p>
    <p><strong><a href="https://daxfoundation.org">The DAX Foundation</a></strong> publishes the protocol. It holds the part a company should not: the mission, and the constraint it answers to — DAX, <em>the preservation and expansion of life, humanity, and consciousness</em> — kept apart from the company that builds the infrastructure. Its site carries the definitions everything else here runs on.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section><div class="shell narrow">
    <h2 class="eyebrow">Working on</h2>
    <div class="maddie">
      <a class="mark" href="https://formaddie.com"><img src="/assets/formaddie-bristlecone.png" width="140" height="145" alt="For Maddie" /></a>
      <p><strong><a href="https://formaddie.com">For Maddie</a></strong> — talk with Maddie and she turns your memories into chapters, emailed to you with the full transcript. It is for keeping a life story. Built at <strong><a href="https://www.obsidiandelta.com">Obsidian Delta</a></strong>, which is the company.</p>
    </div>
  </div></section>

  {listedPosts.length > 0 && (
    <section><div class="shell narrow">
      <h2 class="eyebrow">Writing</h2>
      <ul class="posts">
        {listedPosts.map((p) => (
          <li><a href={`/blog/${p.slug}/`}>{postTitle(p)}</a>{p.description && ` — ${p.description}`}</li>
        ))}
      </ul>
    </div></section>
  )}

  <section><div class="shell narrow">
    <p>If any of this is useful to you, <a href="https://ko-fi.com/jeyanandan">buy me a coffee</a>.</p>
  </div></section>
</Base>

<style is:global>
.hero{padding:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,4.5rem) 0 clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem)}
.lede{font-size:clamp(19px,2.2vw,21px);margin:0}
section + section{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:clamp(2rem,5vw,3rem) 0}
section p:last-child{margin-bottom:0}
section a{text-decoration-thickness:1px;text-underline-offset:.16em}
section a:hover{color:var(--orange)}
section strong{font-weight:600;color:var(--strong)}

/* ---------- working on: the mark beside the line, above it on a phone ---------- */
.maddie{display:flex;gap:1.5rem;align-items:flex-start}
.maddie .mark{flex:0 0 auto;display:block;line-height:0}
.maddie img{display:block;width:140px;max-width:100%;height:auto}
.maddie p{margin:0}
@media (max-width:560px){
  .maddie{flex-direction:column;gap:1rem}
  .maddie img{width:120px}
}

/* ---------- writing ---------- */
.posts{list-style:none;margin:0;padding:0}
.posts li + li{margin-top:.9rem}
</style>
